// ======================================================================================
// 1. BUBBLE SORT
// ======================================================================================

/*

THINKING:

Bubble Sort me har pass me
sabse bada element end me pahuch jata hai.

EXAMPLE:

5 4 3 2 1

Pass 1

5 4 swap

4 5 3 2 1

5 3 swap

4 3 5 2 1

5 2 swap

4 3 2 5 1

5 1 swap

4 3 2 1 5

Sabse bada element end me aa gaya.

-------------------------------------------------

SYNTAX

for(int i=0;i<n-1;i++){

    for(int j=0;j<n-i-1;j++){

        if(arr[j] > arr[j+1]){

            int temp = arr[j];
            arr[j] = arr[j+1];
            arr[j+1] = temp;
        }
    }
}

-------------------------------------------------

PATTERN RECOGNITION

Question me agar:

Adjacent Compare

Swap Neighbours

Bubble Simulation

aise words ho

=> Bubble Sort

-------------------------------------------------

TIME COMPLEXITY

Worst

O(n²)

Best

O(n)

(optimized version)

-------------------------------------------------

INTERVIEW

Rarely asked directly.

Mostly theory me puchte hain.

*/


// ======================================================================================
// 2. SELECTION SORT
// ======================================================================================

/*

THINKING

Har pass me minimum element find karo.

Fir usko front me rakho.

-------------------------------------------------

EXAMPLE

4 2 1 5

Minimum = 1

1 2 4 5

-------------------------------------------------

SYNTAX

for(int i=0;i<n-1;i++){

    int minIndex = i;

    for(int j=i+1;j<n;j++){

        if(arr[j] < arr[minIndex]){

            minIndex = j;
        }
    }

    int temp = arr[i];
    arr[i] = arr[minIndex];
    arr[minIndex] = temp;
}

-------------------------------------------------

TRICK

Find Minimum

Place at Correct Position

=> Selection Sort

-------------------------------------------------

TIME

O(n²)

SPACE

O(1)

-------------------------------------------------

INTERVIEW

Theory Questions

Difference from Bubble Sort

*/


// ======================================================================================
// 3. INSERTION SORT
// ======================================================================================

/*

MOST IMPORTANT SIMPLE SORT

-------------------------------------------------

REAL LIFE EXAMPLE

Cards Arrange Karna

5

3 aaya

3 5

4 aaya

3 4 5

-------------------------------------------------

THINKING

Left part always sorted rahega.

New element ko correct place pe insert karenge.

-------------------------------------------------

SYNTAX

for(int i=1;i<n;i++){

    int current = arr[i];

    int j = i-1;

    while(j>=0 &&
          arr[j] > current){

        arr[j+1] = arr[j];

        j--;
    }

    arr[j+1] = current;
}

-------------------------------------------------

PATTERN RECOGNITION

Question me:

Nearly Sorted

Almost Sorted

Few Elements Wrong Position

=> Insertion Sort

-------------------------------------------------

TIME

Worst

O(n²)

Best

O(n)

-------------------------------------------------

IMPORTANT

Nearly Sorted Array ke liye best.

*/


